Document (dev.stxt.website): Contracts and legal agreements | STXT

	Metadata:
		Last modif: 2026-09-19
		Description: STXT as the source format for contracts and agreements: normative text stays text while parties, dates and amounts are extractable, checkable data.

	Header: Contracts and legal agreements

	Assert >>
		A contract is legal text with data inside: parties, dates, amounts, deadlines.
		In @STXT@ the text remains text, clause by clause, and the data is data,
		in the same document.

	Content >>
		This page is about the **source format** of a contract: the file from which the PDF,
		the next version and the data other systems need all come. It does not replace the signed
		document or the legal process.

	Subheader: A services agreement

	Code >>
		Agreement (com.acme.legal.contract):
			Id: AGR-2026-001
			Title: Technical support services agreement
			Status: Signed
			Effective date: 2026-02-01

			Parties:
				Party: ACME Corp
					Role: Provider
					Registration: B-12345678
				Party: Example Ltd
					Role: Client
					Registration: GB-87654321

			Term:
				Start: 2026-02-01
				End: 2027-01-31

			Payment:
				Fee: 12000
				Currency: EUR
				Billing period: Monthly

			Clauses:
				Clause: Subject matter
					Number: 1
					Text >>
						The Provider shall render to the Client the technical support
						services described in Annex I, within the hours and at the service
						levels established therein.
				Clause: Limitation of liability
					Number: 2
					Text >>
						The total liability of each party shall not exceed the annual amount
						of the contract.

						This limitation shall not apply in case of wilful misconduct or gross
						negligence.
					Internal notes >>
						Standard clause LEG-07, approved by the legal department on
						2025-11-03. Do not modify without legal review.

	Content >>
		In this example we have:

		* **Data**: the parties, the dates and the payment. It is what a billing system or an expiry alert needs.
		* **Clauses**: each one is a node with its title as the value, its number and its text.
		* **Text**: the legal wording of each clause, as is, in a block node that accepts several paragraphs.
		* **Internal notes**: they go inside the clause they refer to, and whoever generates the PDF omits them.

		For example, a program can get these values without reading the contract:

		| Node                | Value        |
		| ------------------- | ------------ |
		| `Term/End`          | `2027-01-31` |
		| `Payment/Fee`       | `12000`      |
		| `Payment/Currency`  | `EUR`        |

	Subheader: The template

	Code >>
		Template (@stxt.template): com.acme.legal.contract
			Structure >>
				Agreement:
					Id: (1)
					Title: (1)
					Status: (1) ENUM [Draft, Signed, Terminated]
					Effective date: (?) DATE
					Parties: (1)
						Party: (2+)
							Role: (1)
							Registration: (?)
					Term: (?)
						Start: (1) DATE
						End: (?) DATE
					Payment: (?)
						Fee: (1) NUMBER
						Currency: (1) ENUM [EUR, USD, GBP]
						Billing period: (?) ENUM [Monthly, Quarterly, Yearly]
					Clauses: (?)
						Clause: (*)
							Number: (?) NATURAL
							Text: (1) TEXT
							Internal notes: (?) TEXT

	Content >>
		The [template](stxt-template-ref) checks the data and does not restrict the wording
		of the clauses, their number or their order.

	Subsubheader: An agreement that does not validate

	Code >>
		# ERROR: this document does not validate
		Agreement (com.acme.legal.contract):
			Id: AGR-2026-002
			Title: Non-disclosure agreement
			Status: Draft
			# An agreement has at least two parties: (2+)
			Parties:
				Party: ACME Corp
					Role: Provider
			Payment:
				# A NUMBER has no thousands separator or symbol
				Fee: 12,000 €
				# `Euros` is not a value of the list
				Currency: Euros
			Clauses:
				# A clause without `Text` is not a clause
				Clause: Confidentiality
					Number: 1

	Subheader: A service level agreement

	Content >>
		An SLA is the case with the most data inside legal text: targets, times and penalties.

	Code >>
		SLA (com.acme.legal.sla):
			Service: Payments platform
			Agreement: AGR-2026-001
			Effective date: 2026-03-01

			Availability:
				Target percentage: 99.9
				Measurement period: Monthly

			Response times:
				Severity: Critical
					Max response minutes: 30
				Severity: High
					Max response minutes: 120
				Severity: Normal
					Max response minutes: 480

			Penalties:
				Penalty: Availability breach
					Condition >>
						Monthly availability below the target.
					Consequence >>
						10 % discount on the invoice of the affected month.

			Legal text >>
				Metrics shall be measured according to the procedures described in the
				technical annex. The parties shall review the targets yearly.

	Content >>
		And its template:

	Code >>
		Template (@stxt.template): com.acme.legal.sla
			Structure >>
				SLA:
					Service: (1)
					Agreement: (?)
					Effective date: (1) DATE
					Availability: (1)
						Target percentage: (1) NUMBER
						Measurement period: (1) ENUM [Monthly, Quarterly]
					Response times: (?)
						Severity: (*)
							Max response minutes: (1) NATURAL
					Penalties: (?)
						Penalty: (*)
							Condition: (1) TEXT
							Consequence: (1) TEXT
					Legal text: (?) TEXT

	Content >>
		`Agreement: AGR-2026-001` links the SLA to its contract. The dashboard that measures the service
		can read the availability target and the response times from the same file
		the parties signed.

	Subheader: How it is used

	Content >>
		* **Versions**: each contract is a file in a repository, and each revision is a diff that shows which clause changed or which date moved.
		* **Standard clauses**: a program compares each clause with the version approved by the legal department, and flags those that differ.
		* **Validation**: `stxt validate --recursive contracts/` ([The command line](tools-cli)) in continuous integration.
		* **Extraction**: the quarter's expiries or the amounts per client come out of the [tree](stxt-tree-ref).
		* **Publishing**: the PDF is generated from the file, without the internal notes.

	Subheader: Limits

	Content >>
		@STXT@ does not provide legal validity, electronic signature or custody.

		It does not interpret the text of the clauses either: "except in case of wilful misconduct" is text,
		and only a person can evaluate it.

		The template does not check consistency between fields (that `End` is later than `Start`,
		or that the contract the SLA cites exists). That is done by the program that walks the repository.

		See also [Corporate documents](use-cases-corporate-docs) and the comparison
		[STXT vs XML](stxt-vs-xml).
